  "notes": [
    "credit and on_credit are attached with default unused-gas weight, so they received more than their 5 Tgas constant (min 6.234 Tgas here); the ratio uses the constant, the worst case when a caller attaches the minimum.",
    "on_credit_call, resolve_credit_call (and ft_resolve_transfer) use unused_gas_weight(0): they get exactly their constant (5 / 10 Tgas attached, confirmed).",
    "credit_call: flagged at 1.97x of its own 5 Tgas budget (2.53 Tgas burnt, including the send fees of its two child receipts). Its 50 Tgas constant = 35 forwarded to ft_on_transfer + 10 for resolve_credit_call + 5 own. In this tx it received 141.4 Tgas (unused-gas weight from a 150 Tgas call); with an ft_transfer_call at the 100 Tgas minimum, the headroom is the 5 Tgas own budget plus its share of leftover gas.",
    "The credit failure counted in credit.failed is K3 case b (unregistered receiver), the intended failure; its burnt gas (panic path) is included.",
    "Small state: each troll holds a handful of accounts. Storage reads and writes on a large trie cost more, so the margins at launch scale will be somewhat lower than these.",
    "ft_resolve_transfer was not exercised (no same-troll ft_transfer_call in these transactions)."
